CRITICAL: Add the missing `handleToggleComplete` function in /app/frontend/src/pages/JobsList.jsx (inside the JobsList component, before renderJobCard). Suggested body:
  const handleToggleComplete = async (job, checked) => {
    try {
      await axios.put(`/jobs/${job.id}`, { completed: checked });
      setJobs(prev => prev.map(j => j.id === job.id ? { ...j, completed: checked } : j));
      toast.success(checked ? 'Job marked complete' : 'Job marked incomplete');
    } catch (e) {
      toast.error('Failed to update job status');
    }
  };
Backend already supports this — PUT /api/jobs/{id} with {completed:true|false} returns 200 and persists (verified via pytest). Once the handler is added, retest Feature 6 & 7 (checkbox click → PUT 200, folder/border/pin turn green, no navigation, reload persists, uncheck reverts to red pin).
